From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000001 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lukasz Madej <l.madej@grinn-global.com>
Date: Thu, 21 May 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fastlogo-ta: guard validator against zero-sized buffer

On platforms where no VPP display output is active at fastlogo TA
initialization time (e.g. AstraSBC booted without HDMI plugged in,
or AstraADA with DSI panel disabled and HDMI unplugged), the
fastlogo TA passes a buffer descriptor with bufSize == 0 down the
shared-memory path.

The actual crash is triggered inside VPP_MapAndValidate_SingleBuffer()
which calls VPP_BUFF_GetHandle() before the validators. With bufSize=0
this invokes TEE_Register_Memory(addr, 0, ...) and TEE_Map_Memory(mem_id=0,
...), producing:

    E/TC: mr_find_region:55 buffer=0xbcd0a000, size=0x00000000
    E/TC: umem_register_memory:645 Cannot find mobj.
    E/TC: umem_map_memory:881 memory id 0x0 is already mapped @ 0x40270000
    E/TC: User mode data-abort at address 0x402a6a10 (translation fault)
    E/LD: Status of TA 1316a183-894d-43fe-9893-bb946ae103f5

Reject zero-sized buffers up-front in VPP_ValidateInput(),
VPP_ValidateOutput() and most importantly in
VPP_MapAndValidate_SingleBuffer() before the buffer handle is acquired.
All existing callers (tee_ta_vpp.c, tee_ta_vpp_shm_cmd.c) already check
the return value, so no behavioural regression is expected on healthy
paths.

This is a local workaround.

Signed-off-by: Lukasz Madej <l.madej@grinn-global.com>
---
 ta/display/ta/vpp/g7/ta_wrapper/common/tee_ta_buffer_check.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

--- a/ta/display/ta/vpp/g7/ta_wrapper/common/tee_ta_buffer_check.c
+++ b/ta/display/ta/vpp/g7/ta_wrapper/common/tee_ta_buffer_check.c
@@ -23,6 +23,10 @@
     TEE_Result res = TEE_ERROR_BAD_PARAMETERS;
     TEE_MemRegion mr;

+    /* workaround: avoid TA data-abort on zero-sized buffer */
+    if (pBuffDec->bufSize == 0)
+        return TEE_ERROR_BAD_PARAMETERS;
+
     if(TEE_SUCCESS != TEE_FindMemRegion(&mr, pBuffDec->bufAddr, pBuffDec->bufSize))
         return res;
     if (TEE_MR_IS_RESTRICTED(&mr))
@@ -37,6 +41,10 @@
     TEE_Result res = TEE_ERROR_BAD_PARAMETERS;
     TEE_MemRegion mr;

+    /* workaround: avoid TA data-abort on zero-sized buffer */
+    if (pBuffDec->bufSize == 0)
+        return TEE_ERROR_BAD_PARAMETERS;
+
     if(TEE_SUCCESS != TEE_FindMemRegion(&mr, pBuffDec->bufAddr, pBuffDec->bufSize))
         return res;
     if (TEE_MR_IS_RESTRICTED(&mr))
@@ -85,6 +93,11 @@
     //memid/phy-addr is passed in pBuffDesc->bufAddr
     shmSize = VPP_SHM_ALIGN_ROUNDUP(pBuffDesc->bufSize);

+    /* workaround: avoid TEE_Register_Memory(addr, 0, ...) which
+     * leads to "Cannot find mobj" and a subsequent TA data-abort */
+    if (shmSize == 0)
+        return TEE_ERROR_BAD_PARAMETERS;
+
     VPP_BUFF_GetHandle(pBuffHandle, (UINT32)pBuffDesc->bufAddr, shmSize, bIsMapToAllInstances, bIsPhyAddrNeeded);

     //Retrieve the value from VPP_BUFF_HANDLE
--
